exit: 0
--- stdout
aethyme — repository navigation, task localization, agent brokering

Usage: aethyme <command> [args...]
       aethyme <command> --help
       aethyme --version | -V

Hot path:
  explore --repo <path> --request "<task>"
                              in-process engine over the local graph store
  explore-summary --from explore.json
                              compact decision surface from a saved answer-json
  verify-targets --repo <path> --from explore.json [--max-targets 2 --max-lines 80]
                              bounded source spans for Explore targets

Content checks:
  content-gate <run|compare-v2|run-v2> <manifest.json>
                              evaluate an uncached Aexeo content change

Agent broker:
  broker start --task <text> --short-name <name>
                              create an isolated worktree + session
  broker status               sessions, overlaps, queue, integration, readiness
  broker submit --session <id>
                              simulate and gate a session
  broker finish --session <id>
                              safely close a completed session
  broker unblock [<id>]       list blockers, or clear one
  broker gc plan|apply        reviewed cleanup of retained state and disk
  broker gc abandon|forget-abandoned
                              archive or retire a pending cleanup journal safely
  broker advanced <verb>      leases, git, gh, review, operations, exec, ...
  hook <event>                agent-surface hook entry point (the plugin's only
                              entry point; reads event JSON on stdin)
  plugin install|status|remove
                              install the agent-surface plugin, or report the
                              plugin/CLI version skew that makes one inert
  update check|plan|execute|apply
                              explicit paired-binary updates; never background
  self-update [--version X.Y.Z]
                              verified, atomic upgrade (= update apply)
  upgrade plan|apply|recover  review, apply, or recover repository migrations

Environments (declared in .aethyme/environments.toml):
  env validate|plan           check profiles statically; preview the host
                              resources a profile would reserve
  env up|down|destroy|sweep   bring this worktree's environment up, destroy it
                              (leases released only after destroy succeeds)
  env park|wake <id>          stop and return capacity units, or wake again
  env exec <id> -- <cmd>      run a command against the environment; never
                              parked while it runs (env touch|pin|unpin)
  env infer [--range R]       minimum profile these changes need (path rules)
  env cache list|prune        content-addressed builds and database templates
  env calibrate               propose units and pool limits from measured
                              footprints (a diff; never written)
  env shared up|redeploy|destroy|list
                              host-wide [[shared]] environments owned by a ref
  env routes                  hostnames the loopback proxy (127.0.0.1:4180)
                              serves; a request to a parked one wakes it
  env status|list|history|logs
                              recorded environments, their phases, history
                              and component logs; host supervisor state

MCP servers (opt-in; <host state>/mcp/services.toml, .aethyme/mcp.toml):
  mcp resolve <name>          launcher chain (pnpm exec, npm exec, npx) to the
                              installed executable; runs and downloads nothing
  mcp connect <name>          become the server (exec: no extra process);
                              --fallback -- <cmd> keeps an agent unblocked
  mcp trust|status|config print
                              trust a repository's .aethyme/mcp.toml; entries,
                              identities, chosen copy; the snippet to paste
                              into an agent (printed, never written)
  mcp manage|intercept|repair|bypass
                              managed servers: launcher shims that route
                              matching calls through connect, agent config
                              repair, and a count of servers that bypass it

Storage (everything Aethyme keeps on this host):
  storage status              per class bytes, budget, what is reclaimable
                              and why not; reads the ledger only
  storage run                 one pass: measure, evict over budget or expired

Agent transcripts (on by default; <host state>/transcripts/settings.toml):
  transcripts status|list     archived and reclaimable bytes, eligible and
                              skipped transcripts with reasons
  transcripts archive --dry-run|--apply
                              compress and move transcripts of closed
                              sessions after N inactive days
                              (Codex: archived_sessions/*.jsonl.zst)
  transcripts restore <id|path>
                              decompress one back, verifying its hash
  transcripts enable|disable  set archiving on or off explicitly for this host

Collaboration (opt-in, experimental; disabled unless [collaboration] enables it):
  collab status|enroll        policy, state root and captures; mint a project ID
  collab capture|gc|context|brief
                              recover captures, reclaim retained data, read
                              bounded context, attach decision briefs

Setup:
  init                        guided setup: certify + scaffold + gates draft
  certify                     read-only certification checks for this repo
  deploy [verify|bridge] [--repo <path>]
                              enroll repository policy and agent guidance

Graph and analysis:
  graph status|units|materialize|refresh|impact|node|callers|...
  task | query | analyze | facts | intents | repo   (each takes --help)

Quality:
  quality inspect [--repo <path>] bounded optional repository-quality analysis
  quality code-shape [--repo <path>] configurable code-shape diagnostics

Deprecated command spellings were removed in v0.8.8; current commands above are canonical.
--- stderr
